  ],
  "contract": "read(2): the kernel writes only the returned number of bytes into the caller's buffer and leaves the rest untouched.",
  "observed": "Asterinas ramfs and exFAT overwrite the caller's buffer past the returned count (zeros up to the page-cache capacity), even when the read returns 0 at EOF.",
